From: avlo-py-build <py-build@avlo.local>
Subject: [PATCH] AVLO: 0008 snapshot half — getExpectedKeys 5-entry table

getExpectedKeys() hardcodes the first hiwire regular-table entries in
boot allocation order, and the "js" registration (deleted by 0008)
was what interned jsglobals (slot 1) plus a trailing {} (slot 6).
Post-0008 the table is [null, public_api, API, scheduleCallback, API]
— verified empirically against a live 314.0.2 boot by the py-build
harness snapshot section, which walks Module.__hiwire_get and dumps
the real table on any mismatch (re-derive there after any
boot-sequence change). Without this rewrite serializeHiwireState dies
stringifying public_api (circular Module.FS root) against the stale
jsglobals expectation. Capture and restore share the list; the
client's buildId gate rejects snapshots captured under any other
layout.

diff --git a/src/js/snapshot.ts b/src/js/snapshot.ts
index 07f243a..b513533 100644
--- a/src/js/snapshot.ts
+++ b/src/js/snapshot.ts
@@ -4,15 +4,15 @@ declare var Module: any;
 
 /** @private */
 API.getExpectedKeys = function () {
-  return [
-    null,
-    API.config.jsglobals,
-    API.public_api,
-    API,
-    scheduleCallback,
-    API,
-    {},
-  ];
+  // AVLO (0008b): with register_js_module("js", jsglobals) gone (0008),
+  // jsglobals is never interned and the trailing {} entry that registration
+  // produced is gone too — the post-boot table is exactly these five entries.
+  // Empirically re-derived against a live 314.0.2 boot (the py-build harness
+  // snapshot section walks Module.__hiwire_get and dumps the real table on
+  // any mismatch — re-derive there after any boot-sequence change).
+  // syncUpSnapshotLoad2 re-interns this same list on restore; the client's
+  // buildId gate rejects snapshots captured under any other layout.
+  return [null, API.public_api, API, scheduleCallback, API];
 };
 
 // Symbol used in our serializer to get the access list
